From 8a1237c3e17d91e3bacaf947b788f3e4af54f07a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dazhanzheng <1365950682@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:20:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(harmony): deterministic model unload + prepack toggle

Add explicit-destroy handles for OnlineRecognizer and OfflinePunctuation
(mirroring the OnlineStreamHandle pattern from patch 0006), exposing
destroyOnlineRecognizer / destroyOfflinePunctuation to ArkTS with idempotent
Close() that is safe against the NAPI finalizer. Without this, clearing the
ArkTS pool only drops references and the recognizer/punctuation ORT session
memory (~150+ MB) is reclaimed only at GC, so SpeechRecognizeSdk.unloadModel
cannot actually free memory. Verified on 9020: unloadModel now frees ~283 MB.

Also add a deployment-time prepack toggle with no C-API/ABI change: session.cc
parses an inline provider config ("cpu;DisablePrepacking=1") and applies
session.disable_prepacking, so an ArkTS-level AsrConfig flag can trade
inference throughput for lower cold-load latency and peak memory.
